From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:01:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: let clients say what their glass is for and hear its
 material

kestrel_glass_v1 gives a surface with glass a glass object. Through it a
client says whether the glass is the base of a window or a transient
surface such as a popover, which follows the person's choice for panels
and menus, and may ask for Luca or Maris instead of the person's choice.
Maris is always granted, Luca too, and then blurs only the wallpaper
whenever the person's Luca does. The client hears which material its
glass has, so it can leave out its own tint over Maris, whose surface
colour is already the whole surface.

Upstream-Status: luft-only Kestrel's private kestrel_glass_v1 protocol
